<title>USA: Northern States arm signs Indonesia contract.</title>
<headline>Northern States arm signs Indonesia contract.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>NRG Energy Inc, a unit of Northern States Power Co, said Thursday it signed a power contract with PT Perusahaan Listrik Negara (PLN), the state-owned Indonesian electric company, to build, own and operate a 400-megawatt, coal-fired power station.</p>
<p>NRG Energy will have a 45 percent stake in the project in Cilegon, West Java, Indonesia.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>NRG will operate and maintain the power plant for the 30-year life of the project. Construction is due to begin in mid-1997 with the facility fully operational by 2000.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
